    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This cardigan uses the same "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "granny-sq-g182"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "granny square"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " as the pullover, assembled with a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "flat-join-g182"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "flat join"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and finished with a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "dc-border-g182"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "dc border"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " along the full front opening."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The left and right front panels each run from shoulder to hem. There is no button band construction: the dc border provides all the edge finishing needed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Square count guide"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "At size M the back panel is 4 squares wide x 4 tall. Each front panel is 2 squares wide x 4 tall. Each sleeve is 3 squares wide x 4 tall. Total squares at size M: 52."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Adjust width by adding or removing one square column per panel. Keep front and back column counts consistent so the shoulder seams align."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials (size M)",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Aran yarn",
              "qty": "850 yards"
            },
            {
              "name": "5 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            },
            {
              "name": "Rust-proof pins for blocking",
              "qty": "20 or more"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Making the squares"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work each granny square to 15 cm following the standard three-round construction: magic ring, four corner clusters with ch-2 spaces, two further rounds adding clusters along each side. Block every square flat before joining."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly order"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join back panel squares in a grid. Join each front panel separately. Seam back to fronts at shoulders. Attach sleeve panels at the armhole edges. Seam side and sleeve edges."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Border"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Starting at one lower front corner, work the dc border continuously around the lower hem, up the right front, around the neck, down the left front and along the hem. Work 3 dc into each outer corner to keep the corners flat. Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The granny square vest drops the sleeves and shortens the body for a lighter layering piece."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
